  "semantics": [
    "Sequence is bounded reservation index 0..63, exported in strictly increasing order; incomplete slots are omitted, so gaps are allowed.",
    "Only fully written records with acquire-observed ready markers are exported. Capture marker is published last and only if every registry write succeeds.",
    "Fixed 64-slot storage; no pointers, packet contents, addresses, network identifiers, strings, allocations, logging or registry access in trace append.",
    "IRQ causes and masks reuse CPU local/state values, with no additional hardware reads. ICT-empty and invalid-CSR events use literal zero for unread cause registers.",
    "Command send/wait/return records cover only the first two admitted synchronous startup commands. Other event kinds cover the bounded startup context until snapshot.",
    "First failure or startup cleanup/success freezes and snapshots trace in safe startup context. Snapshot is sticky across retries; already-in-flight producers may be omitted and counted incomplete if their reserved slot was visible.",
    "dropped counts append attempts rejected by capacity, saturating at UINT32_MAX; incomplete counts visible reserved slots not ready at snapshot. Late producer reservation may fall after the snapshot cutoff.",
    "Registry publication failure leaves captured absent; no partial publication is claimed complete.",
    "errno/thread_result are uint32 representations; no runtime Wi-Fi success claim."
  ]
